\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The FJ model on the directed cycle of Figure~\ref {fig:networks}(a) when agent~$1$ is the only prejudiced agent ($\lambda _1 < 1$, $\lambda _i = 1$ for $i \neq  1$), and its augmented graph. Unlabelled edges have weight $1$. (a)~The prejudice $u_1$ enters agent~$1$ as an external input, with weight $1-\lambda _1$; this arrow is not an edge of $G$. (b)~The input becomes the virtual agent $1'$ (dashed), which is stubborn and keeps the opinion $u_1$. The virtual agents $2', \dots  , 6'$ are stubborn agents that nobody listens to, and are not drawn.}}{14}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
